# Globally ignored Trivy checks for this dev/demo project.
#
# These IDs flag postgres/redis/zipkin deployments because those third-party
# images require a writable root filesystem and their "correct" non-root
# setup is image-family specific (Bitnami runs as UID 1001, Alpine variants
# run as root by default). Our own code (k8s/inventory-deployment.yaml and
# k8s/products-deployment.yaml) ENFORCES readOnlyRootFilesystem + runAsUser
# 10001 + drop ALL capabilities + seccompProfile=RuntimeDefault — the
# suppression is only load-bearing for the infra pods.
#
# Production migration path (out of scope here):
#   - Swap postgres/redis to Bitnami images (non-root by default, UID 1001)
#   - Mount emptyDir at /var/lib/{postgresql,redis} and /tmp for writable
#     state under readOnlyRootFilesystem: true
#   - Remove these entries.
AVD-KSV-0014
AVD-KSV-0118
